WEBVTT

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:04.410
Hey, everyone, we're going to start
Kaleido Star.

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:07.180
When you watch Kaleido Star,
please keep your room brightly lit,

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:09.410
and sit as far from the TV as you can.

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:14.110
Well, well, well. Do you have siblings?

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:16.020
Nice older brothers or sisters.

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:17.810
Or darling younger brothers or sisters?

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:20.180
Very soon, I'm going to be an older sister.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:24.420
Is it a boy? Or is it a girl?
I should be very happy, but...

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:28.350
I'm a little anxious. I am. I am.

00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:35.770
<i>The dream everyone is looking for
must be someplace</i>

00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:35.770
<i>Dare mo sagashiteru yume wa kitto aru</i>

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:38.270
<i>It has to be somewhere</i>

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:38.270
<i>Dokoka ni aru</i>

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:45.980
<i>Until your dream comes true someday,
you're not alone</i>

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:45.980
<i>Negai ga itsuka kanau made hitori ja nai</i>

00:00:54.020 --> 00:01:00.330
<i>Remember how I used to say
I could make it to the end?</i>

00:00:54.020 --> 00:01:00.330
<i>Saigo made yareru to ittetane</i>

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:06.700
<i>I must have been pretending to be tough</i>

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:06.700
<i>Kitto tsuyogatte itanda</i>

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:15.410
<i>Everything I did was reckless
and it never got me anywhere</i>

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:15.410
<i>Itsudatte muchabakka de
zutto karamawari de</i>

00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:21.910
<i>But you alone were always beside me</i>

00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:21.910
<i>Dakedo anata dake ga soba ni ita</i>

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:28.660
<i>The dream everyone is looking for
must be somewhere</i>

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:28.660
<i>Daremo sagashiteru yume wa kitto aru</i>

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:31.260
<i>You can start going forward</i>

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:31.260
<i>Aruki daseru</i>

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:36.800
<i>From this moment, something will start</i>

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:36.800
<i>Koko kara nani kaga hajimaru</i>

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:38.830
<i>I want to believe that</i>

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:38.830
<i>Shinjite itai</i>

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:46.340
<i>The light I haven't seen yet
is beaming toward the promised place</i>

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:46.340
<i>Mada minu hikari yakusoku no
basho e to tsuzuite yuku</i>

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:56.810
<i>Until your dream comes true someday,
you're not alone</i>

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:56.810
<i>Negai ga itsuka kanau made hitori ja naisa</i>

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:05.120
I know. But, you don't need to worry.

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:08.260
I'm going to find a room where
I can live with my friends,

00:02:08.260 --> 00:02:11.320
and we've decided to create
our own company together.

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:16.440
I know, I'm sure it'll be hard,
but I want to give it a try.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:18.800
So, I don't think I'll go back
there for a while.

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:25.310
Oh... Really?

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:27.800
Er... Well...
What should I say?

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:29.480
Congratulations...

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:31.880
Oh, that's why they say "Congratulations"
on occasions like these.

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:34.590
I'm happy for you, Mother.

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:36.660
What? Really?

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:38.350
Somehow, I sound weird?

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:40.290
Well, I'm acting the same as usual.

00:02:42.460 --> 00:02:42.660
Amazing Family Ties

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:45.400
"Amazing Family Ties"

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:45.400
Amazing Family Ties

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:48.300
Amazing Family Ties

00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:49.470
All right.

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:52.800
As of today, a new life will start.

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:54.500
A new...

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:58.480
I should be happy.

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:00.970
But why do I feel this way?

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:04.290
You don't need to look so sad.

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:06.050
I will come with you, Sora.

00:03:06.050 --> 00:03:07.420
So, you're coming with me?

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:10.390
Of course. So, feel easy.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:12.860
If you EVER peep into Mia or Anna's bath,

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:15.230
you're going to immediately
be food for Jonathan!

00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:16.560
Oh... Yes!

00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:18.160
Thank you for waiting.

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:19.800
You're late. You're late.

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:20.900
Do you have everything with you?

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:21.740
Yes.

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:22.530
Then, let's go.

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:24.670
Until we find our own place,

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:26.210
we'll take your offer and stay with your family.

00:03:26.210 --> 00:03:28.640
Everyone in my family is also
looking forward to seeing you guys.

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:30.970
Miss Sarah...

00:03:31.550 --> 00:03:33.410
So, all you guys are also finally heading out.

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:35.150
Where are you going, Miss Sarah?

00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:37.950
I'm leaving for training, of course.

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:40.120
Bye...

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:41.960
Training?

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:43.530
She left for training for singing. Didn't she?

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:46.560
Somehow, she looked like
she left for martial arts training.

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:49.500
Since it's Miss Sarah, it could be the case.

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:54.400
But, thanks to Ken's family,
I was really saved.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.540
My grandma felt relieved.

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:58.670
After all, a newspaper
already printed an article

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:01.470
saying that after Kaleido Stage's
owner changed, the cast quit.

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:05.380
There is no way that I can turn
young girls adrift into the streets.

00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:07.350
Wow, you sound very manly.

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:08.850
Don't tease me.

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:09.680
Sorry.

00:04:11.420 --> 00:04:12.480
Sora...

00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:15.390
Are you worried about something?

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:17.920
What? Oh... No. It's nothing like that.

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:19.090
SORA!

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:19.790
What?

00:04:19.790 --> 00:04:20.990
Your suitcase!

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:24.830
Oh, I remember...

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:25.870
Before you come to my house,

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:28.140
there is something I want you
to be prepared for...

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:29.100
Be prepared for?

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:30.910
I've already spoken
strictly to her about it...

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:32.370
But, my younger sister is especially...

00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:33.670
This is it.

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:36.210
Wow...

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:38.740
It's like a park.

00:04:39.350 --> 00:04:41.650
I know. My father built it.

00:04:41.650 --> 00:04:44.150
Your father? Amazing!

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:45.450
Oh, I know. And, about my younger sister...

00:04:51.130 --> 00:04:52.160
Wow!

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:54.290
It's Anna! It's really Anna!

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:55.490
Here!

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:56.960
Hold it, hold it!

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:58.770
Pose, pose!

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:06.270
My younger sister, Lucy, is a big Anna fan.

00:05:06.270 --> 00:05:07.180
She doesn't think it's funny.

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:07.970
Ken!

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:11.310
It's not nice to keep them outside for so long.

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:13.170
Here, hurry. Come inside quick.

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:14.580
Go inside.

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:15.880
My mom is...

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:17.480
Hey...

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:21.320
Ben! Everyone is here!

00:05:22.790 --> 00:05:24.320
It's nice to meet you.

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:26.390
Oh, come in.

00:05:26.390 --> 00:05:28.730
Really, all you do is rest.

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:29.830
You're wrong.

00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:31.570
I'm trying to get the idea
for a new design of...

00:05:31.570 --> 00:05:32.900
Here, move, move.

00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:34.600
Here, please, please.

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:38.340
My father designs furniture.

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:41.710
Don't be so modest, have a seat.

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:43.000
I'll make coffee.

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:44.550
Oh, thank you.

00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:45.380
Here, Anna.

00:05:45.380 --> 00:05:46.540
Hurry, hurry.

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:48.640
Have a seat, quick.

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:51.580
Wow! Anna is sitting on our couch!

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:52.550
Ook Ook!

00:05:54.190 --> 00:05:55.120
Somehow...

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:57.090
Anna is different
from what I had in my mind.

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:58.560
I'm very sorry.

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:00.560
So, this was no good either?

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:01.490
Definitely.

00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:05.790
I wonder if posing as a monkey
is too ordinary...

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:06.900
Good!

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:08.630
Oh, it's good!

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:10.070
This is the last one.

00:06:10.540 --> 00:06:12.410
I'll leave your luggage here.

00:06:12.410 --> 00:06:13.370
Oh, thank you...

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:14.740
Wow...

00:06:20.550 --> 00:06:22.350
This room is so adorable.

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:23.550
Sorry.

00:06:23.550 --> 00:06:26.550
This used to be a kid's room.
So, it's kind of messy, but...

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:28.590
Not at all. It's wonderful.

00:06:28.590 --> 00:06:30.680
Did you design this, too?

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:33.360
Yes, if you find anything you like,

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:35.230
you can take it with you
when you find your own place.

00:06:35.230 --> 00:06:36.420
Really?

00:06:36.630 --> 00:06:37.030
Here.

00:06:37.030 --> 00:06:38.560
This time hold this.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:42.540
Ah! I still want take more pictures of Anna!

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:44.900
Well, take it easy until dinner.

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:44.900
Ah! I still want take more pictures of Anna!

00:06:45.470 --> 00:06:47.040
Anna!

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:48.880
I think we should find our apartment quickly.

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:49.740
Yes, we should.

00:06:51.950 --> 00:06:53.280
A kid's room...

00:06:56.890 --> 00:07:01.650
Once my father and mother's
real child is born, l...

00:07:04.130 --> 00:07:05.520
Sora, what's wrong?

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:07.560
You've been depressed for a while.

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:09.050
What? I don't think I am.

00:07:11.270 --> 00:07:13.030
When did he sneak in?!

00:07:13.030 --> 00:07:13.830
Sora?

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:17.200
He's gone.

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:20.310
You!

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:21.740
What's wrong, Sora?

00:07:21.740 --> 00:07:22.770
Is it a bug or something?

00:07:25.450 --> 00:07:26.240
Sora!

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:27.850
What's the matter with you?

00:07:29.480 --> 00:07:30.380
I GOT YOU!

00:07:33.320 --> 00:07:35.080
I'm sorry for making all that noise.

00:07:35.560 --> 00:07:36.790
How shall I say this?

00:07:36.790 --> 00:07:39.160
But to show you how sorry I feel,
let me help you prepare dinner.

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:40.130
Us too...

00:07:40.130 --> 00:07:41.560
Oh, thank you.

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:43.060
But you don't need to worry.

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:44.830
Our place is always noisy, and...

00:07:45.430 --> 00:07:48.740
Ken used to jump off the bunk bed
often when he was a child too.

00:07:48.740 --> 00:07:49.570
He did?

00:07:49.570 --> 00:07:52.040
Yes. He'd say that he'd be a Kaleido Star.

00:07:52.310 --> 00:07:55.540
But, that boy, since he was a child,
his heart was weak, and...

00:07:55.540 --> 00:08:00.050
Even so, it wasn't so bad that he
had any problems living a normal life.

00:08:00.050 --> 00:08:02.540
So, he had a hard time giving up.

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:04.590
I understand how he feels.

00:08:04.590 --> 00:08:06.450
But, as his mother, I couldn't
let him do what he really wanted.

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:09.220
Even now, I'm nervous,

00:08:09.220 --> 00:08:12.760
worrying that he may say he wants
to appear on stage one of these days.

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:15.230
KEN! Give me my camera back!

00:08:15.230 --> 00:08:16.130
No!

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:19.630
As long as you have this,
you'll keep chasing after Anna.

00:08:19.870 --> 00:08:22.100
What's wrong with it?
I'll brag about it to my friends.

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:24.410
Then, you should invite your friends here.

00:08:24.410 --> 00:08:25.570
She is the real Anna.

00:08:25.570 --> 00:08:26.740
Oh, that's a good idea!

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:28.800
Dad, please don't say anything unnecessary.

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:31.510
I have a younger brother.

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:33.650
I did the same. We used to fight all the time.

00:08:33.650 --> 00:08:34.480
Me too.

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:36.510
When I had a quarrel with my mom,
it was rough.

00:08:37.190 --> 00:08:39.480
At our house... I don't think we ever fought.

00:08:39.650 --> 00:08:40.680
What?

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:42.960
Now, let's have dinner.

00:08:54.870 --> 00:08:55.730
Sora...

00:08:56.100 --> 00:08:57.010
Ken...

00:08:57.010 --> 00:08:58.370
Can't sleep?

00:08:58.370 --> 00:08:59.970
I was just enjoying the cool weather.

00:09:00.170 --> 00:09:02.140
Sorry my place is so noisy.

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:04.350
No. I think it's very nice.

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:08.040
Everyone says whatever is on their minds.
It's like a real family.

00:09:08.450 --> 00:09:12.410
Even though they're your adopted parents,
aren't they your real family?

00:09:12.590 --> 00:09:15.610
Yes, sure. What am I saying?

00:09:15.890 --> 00:09:16.960
I thought so.

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:19.090
I think you're worried
about something, aren't you?

00:09:19.330 --> 00:09:21.360
Oh... Not at all.

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:23.600
On the contrary,
there's something to celebrate.

00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:25.120
My mother is going to have a baby.

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:28.240
Really?

00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:29.640
You're going to have a sibling.

00:09:29.640 --> 00:09:30.510
Congratulations.

00:09:30.510 --> 00:09:31.490
Thank you.

00:09:33.810 --> 00:09:35.780
They couldn't have a baby for so long.

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:39.180
I thought they weren't having kids
because they were concerned about me.

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:41.780
And if they were, I thought I'd feel so bad...

00:09:41.780 --> 00:09:42.820
But I feel better now.

00:09:42.820 --> 00:09:46.780
When my younger sister was born,
I remember I felt a little sad.

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:48.820
This is something natural,

00:09:48.820 --> 00:09:51.990
but both my parents devoted
all their energies to my newborn sister.

00:09:52.560 --> 00:09:54.400
So I used to say unreasonable
things on purpose,

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:56.590
and gave my mother and father a hard time.

00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:00.500
But I'm afraid I can never do
anything like that;

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:03.910
having a serious fight,
or speaking my mind to them.

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:07.570
I'm afraid of destroying our family bonds.

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:10.410
I don't think it's like that.

00:10:10.410 --> 00:10:11.210
Okay...

00:10:11.550 --> 00:10:13.410
Please tell me anything.

00:10:13.410 --> 00:10:16.750
I... think I can be a family if it's with you.

00:10:20.490 --> 00:10:21.690
You're right.

00:10:21.690 --> 00:10:23.950
We're like family, you and me.

00:10:24.260 --> 00:10:24.790
Sora...

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:24.960
Mia and Anna too.

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:24.960
Sora...

00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:26.230
Mia and Anna too.

00:10:26.230 --> 00:10:27.020
What?

00:10:27.260 --> 00:10:30.920
We're going to make our own Kaleido Stage.

00:10:31.170 --> 00:10:32.860
It's no time to be depressed!

00:10:33.130 --> 00:10:34.040
First thing tomorrow,

00:10:34.040 --> 00:10:36.300
I will try hard to find an apartment!

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:37.370
Well, good night, Ken.

00:10:37.370 --> 00:10:37.970
No... I didn't mean it like that.

00:10:37.370 --> 00:10:37.970
Well, good night, Ken.

00:10:37.970 --> 00:10:39.600
No... I didn't mean it like that.

00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:41.940
I know...

00:10:41.940 --> 00:10:45.050
Since I'm with everyone,
I should be able to keep going.

00:10:45.050 --> 00:10:48.450
Also, I want to show my performances
to both my mother and father.

00:10:49.980 --> 00:10:51.380
Please be my friends forever too.

00:10:55.520 --> 00:10:57.330
That Sora...

00:10:57.330 --> 00:11:00.190
She gets rougher and rougher with me.

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:04.520
The Empress...

00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:06.730
We're leaving!

00:11:15.080 --> 00:11:16.010
Aren't you tired?

00:11:16.510 --> 00:11:17.500
No.

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:36.830
A penthouse with a yard...

00:11:36.830 --> 00:11:37.730
Amazing!

00:11:37.730 --> 00:11:38.530
Too expensive.

00:11:38.970 --> 00:11:41.140
A standalone house in the suburbs
might not be a bad idea!

00:11:41.140 --> 00:11:41.930
Too far.

00:11:42.440 --> 00:11:43.270
How about here?

00:11:43.270 --> 00:11:44.970
It's less expensive and it looks like
it's in a convenient location.

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:45.810
Hm...

00:11:45.810 --> 00:11:46.600
No.

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:47.780
Mr. Policeman.

00:11:47.780 --> 00:11:49.140
Why is it not good?

00:11:49.140 --> 00:11:51.870
This place was robbed before.

00:11:52.050 --> 00:11:53.280
What...

00:11:53.280 --> 00:11:55.580
It's not easy to find a nice place.

00:11:56.850 --> 00:11:58.680
Not necessarily.

00:12:02.090 --> 00:12:02.760
This is it.

00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:02.920
It's old.

00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:02.920
This is it.

00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:03.550
It's old.

00:12:03.960 --> 00:12:06.060
It's not as bad as it looks.

00:12:06.060 --> 00:12:08.430
The rent is cheap,
it's in a convenient location, and...

00:12:08.430 --> 00:12:10.520
I live here too.

00:12:10.630 --> 00:12:11.830
Miss Kate!

00:12:12.170 --> 00:12:13.070
This is it.

00:12:13.070 --> 00:12:13.930
Wow...

00:12:14.370 --> 00:12:15.200
What do you think?

00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:16.740
I think it's pretty good.

00:12:16.740 --> 00:12:17.570
I told you.

00:12:17.570 --> 00:12:19.510
The inside is cleaner than I thought.

00:12:19.510 --> 00:12:20.870
It's pretty big.

00:12:22.080 --> 00:12:23.040
Oh...

00:12:24.780 --> 00:12:26.480
The view is good, and...

00:12:26.480 --> 00:12:27.310
Yeah, it motivates me.

00:12:27.380 --> 00:12:28.280
Yes, it does.

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:30.220
I think this place is good.

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:31.050
Me too.

00:12:31.050 --> 00:12:32.080
Then it's settled.

00:12:33.190 --> 00:12:36.190
From here, we're going to start up
our own Kaleido Stage.

00:12:36.190 --> 00:12:39.020
By all means!

00:12:39.590 --> 00:12:41.830
Since I live just below,

00:12:41.830 --> 00:12:43.930
just let me know if there's anything you need.

00:12:43.930 --> 00:12:45.500
Isn't it perfect?

00:12:45.500 --> 00:12:48.330
Everyone, why don't we have
coffee or something in my room?

00:12:48.570 --> 00:12:49.660
In YOUR room?

00:12:50.400 --> 00:12:52.900
It's a little messy,
but don't let it bother you.

00:12:53.170 --> 00:12:55.640
I'm the one who usually
cleans up this place.

00:12:55.740 --> 00:12:57.610
A perfect place...

00:12:57.610 --> 00:13:02.020
There's the distinct possibility
we'll have to clean Miss Kate's room too.

00:13:02.020 --> 00:13:04.610
Well... I guess there is
no such thing as the perfect deal.

00:13:05.320 --> 00:13:06.950
Jerry, where's the coffee?

00:13:07.690 --> 00:13:08.480
Jerry?

00:13:08.860 --> 00:13:11.230
So, Mr. Policeman's name is Jerry.

00:13:11.230 --> 00:13:12.130
It's so cute.

00:13:12.130 --> 00:13:13.350
It's too good for him.

00:13:13.430 --> 00:13:14.800
Who cares what kind of name I have?!

00:13:14.800 --> 00:13:15.760
Jerry!

00:13:14.800 --> 00:13:15.760
Who cares what kind of name I have?!

00:13:16.460 --> 00:13:18.600
Who knew we would find a place so fast?

00:13:18.600 --> 00:13:20.170
Yeah, we're lucky.

00:13:20.170 --> 00:13:23.270
Lucy will be disappointed to lose you.

00:13:23.270 --> 00:13:24.670
Shall we leave Anna alone there?

00:13:24.670 --> 00:13:25.470
Don't!

00:13:26.840 --> 00:13:28.570
Someone's waiting in front of the house.

00:13:29.840 --> 00:13:30.670
Oh, Sora...

00:13:31.810 --> 00:13:32.710
Sora...

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:34.720
Father... Mother...

00:13:34.720 --> 00:13:35.980
What?

00:13:37.490 --> 00:13:38.320
Thank you.

00:13:38.320 --> 00:13:39.120
You're welcome.

00:13:39.590 --> 00:13:42.790
Since she came here all the way from Japan
in that kind of condition,

00:13:42.790 --> 00:13:45.050
I wonder if they came here to
take Sora back with them.

00:13:45.160 --> 00:13:47.530
After we finally found our own apartment...

00:13:48.100 --> 00:13:49.600
You surprised me...

00:13:49.600 --> 00:13:51.070
'Cause all of a sudden
you were waiting for me.

00:13:51.070 --> 00:13:54.100
When we went to your dormitory,
they said they had no idea where you went.

00:13:54.100 --> 00:13:55.200
So it took a while to find this place.

00:13:55.200 --> 00:13:58.910
Oh, sorry. I meant to call you later.

00:13:58.910 --> 00:14:01.810
Anyway, are you okay
coming all the way here?

00:14:02.040 --> 00:14:03.340
I'm fine.

00:14:03.340 --> 00:14:06.210
Your mother insisted on coming here.

00:14:06.210 --> 00:14:07.320
Because...

00:14:07.320 --> 00:14:09.220
I was concerned after
we talked on the phone.

00:14:09.350 --> 00:14:12.520
Did I sound that bad? It's weird.

00:14:12.520 --> 00:14:14.590
If you're worried about me, I'm fine.

00:14:14.590 --> 00:14:18.030
Over the phone, I can't tell
whether you're doing all right or not.

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:19.990
Oh, really?

00:14:19.990 --> 00:14:22.620
Oh, by the way,
we found an apartment today.

00:14:22.860 --> 00:14:25.570
That policeman Father met referred it to us.

00:14:25.570 --> 00:14:26.360
So don't you feel relieved?

00:14:26.900 --> 00:14:29.500
And there's even a doctor
living on the floor below us.

00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:31.110
Her name is Miss Kate.

00:14:31.110 --> 00:14:33.240
I think Mr. Policeman
is secretly in love with her.

00:14:33.240 --> 00:14:33.440
Sora...

00:14:33.240 --> 00:14:33.440
I think Mr. Policeman
is secretly in love with her.

00:14:33.440 --> 00:14:34.770
Sora...

00:14:35.580 --> 00:14:38.240
Why don't you come back
to Japan for a while?

00:14:40.510 --> 00:14:43.050
Because, if you quit Kaleido Stage,

00:14:43.050 --> 00:14:45.140
I know you will have a hard time
making a living.

00:14:45.250 --> 00:14:47.120
If you're worried about that,
my friends and I will...

00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:49.790
Even though you're going to
create your own Kaleido Stage,

00:14:49.790 --> 00:14:54.160
if you rest for a little while in Japan,
you will get new ideas.

00:14:54.360 --> 00:14:57.670
And if you do that, we don't need
to worry about you every day either.

00:14:57.670 --> 00:14:58.500
So, can you...

00:14:58.500 --> 00:15:02.200
Before long, you won't
have time to worry about me.

00:15:02.200 --> 00:15:03.570
Once you have your own child...

00:15:04.470 --> 00:15:06.170
Oh...

00:15:06.610 --> 00:15:07.700
Sora...

00:15:09.080 --> 00:15:11.010
Don't be silly!

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:13.140
Why wouldn't we worry about you?!

00:15:13.910 --> 00:15:16.080
We'd never be like that!

00:15:17.280 --> 00:15:18.310
Sorry...

00:15:19.050 --> 00:15:19.850
No...

00:15:20.320 --> 00:15:23.190
I didn't come here to say this.

00:15:23.190 --> 00:15:25.620
I should also apologize. Sorry...

00:15:27.630 --> 00:15:28.650
Midori?

00:15:30.130 --> 00:15:31.190
Mother...

00:15:31.830 --> 00:15:34.670
Oh, dear! Ken, call an ambulance.

00:15:34.670 --> 00:15:35.500
Yes!

00:15:35.500 --> 00:15:37.000
Ben, get a car ready!

00:15:37.000 --> 00:15:38.610
Midori, be strong!

00:15:38.610 --> 00:15:39.640
Please lie down.

00:15:39.640 --> 00:15:41.610
The ambulance will be here soon.

00:15:43.140 --> 00:15:45.240
Midori! Midori!

00:15:47.520 --> 00:15:49.140
Mother!

00:15:51.020 --> 00:15:52.790
A Caesarean section?

00:15:52.790 --> 00:15:54.620
But she's only seven months pregnant...

00:15:54.620 --> 00:15:57.460
It's an emergency situation.
There are no other alternatives.

00:15:58.230 --> 00:15:59.730
Hey, Ben.

00:15:59.730 --> 00:16:02.100
Why don't you calm down a bit?

00:16:02.100 --> 00:16:03.500
Oh... Yeah...

00:16:04.800 --> 00:16:05.970
What shall I do?

00:16:05.970 --> 00:16:07.440
Sora, be strong.

00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:08.770
I'm sure that she'll be all right.

00:16:08.770 --> 00:16:11.210
It's because I said something terrible to her...

00:16:11.210 --> 00:16:12.040
That's why my mother...

00:16:12.040 --> 00:16:13.940
It's not your fault.

00:16:13.940 --> 00:16:15.810
No, it is my fault.

00:16:16.310 --> 00:16:18.650
I just thought once my mother has a baby...

00:16:18.650 --> 00:16:21.880
There would be no room for me...

00:16:21.880 --> 00:16:25.520
I know my mother is
so happy about having a baby.

00:16:25.520 --> 00:16:27.790
But I can't feel happy for her
from the bottom of my heart,

00:16:27.790 --> 00:16:29.360
and I don't like being like this.

00:16:29.360 --> 00:16:31.530
And I thought if I go back to Japan now,

00:16:31.530 --> 00:16:35.090
my mother will sense that part of me
that I don't like.

00:16:35.560 --> 00:16:38.760
That's why... I said something like that.

00:16:39.870 --> 00:16:43.440
Mother was trying so hard to be a family...

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:47.460
But l... I broke it.

00:16:50.440 --> 00:16:51.240
Sora.

00:16:51.910 --> 00:16:56.350
Aren't you worried about your mother
from the bottom of your heart right now?

00:16:56.350 --> 00:16:59.620
You're wishing that she will
have the baby without any problems.

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:01.210
Don't you think that's
what family is all about?

00:17:01.820 --> 00:17:03.980
All of you are a real family.

00:17:04.490 --> 00:17:06.690
No matter what happens,
your family will never fall apart.

00:17:08.060 --> 00:17:10.360
Both your mother and her baby
are trying hard...

00:17:11.370 --> 00:17:12.660
Let's cheer them on.

00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:16.660
Yes. Thank you, Ken.

00:17:21.980 --> 00:17:25.080
Mother, please hold on.

00:17:25.080 --> 00:17:26.740
And, you too, baby...

00:17:27.110 --> 00:17:31.480
Please... Please be born safely...

00:17:32.250 --> 00:17:34.810
I'm waiting for you.

00:17:48.140 --> 00:17:50.190
It's a girl.

00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:56.430
Your mother is calm. She's resting now.

00:17:57.880 --> 00:17:59.810
Thank you very much.

00:18:04.620 --> 00:18:06.120
She's so tiny.

00:18:06.120 --> 00:18:07.820
Your mother was only
seven months pregnant.

00:18:08.490 --> 00:18:09.920
But she's fine.

00:18:11.030 --> 00:18:12.660
You were the same.

00:18:12.660 --> 00:18:13.490
What?

00:18:13.490 --> 00:18:16.050
You were in an incubator like she is now.

00:18:16.900 --> 00:18:21.440
Back then, your mother and father
were so worried about you,

00:18:21.440 --> 00:18:22.930
and they blamed themselves too.

00:18:23.840 --> 00:18:25.530
Unable to hold you for a while,

00:18:26.340 --> 00:18:28.710
every time when they saw you
in the incubator,

00:18:28.880 --> 00:18:32.370
they used to tell you to be strong
and grow up healthy.

00:18:32.580 --> 00:18:35.710
I remember very well that they
were cheering for you like that.

00:18:37.550 --> 00:18:40.890
When you told me you wanted
to join Kaleido Stage,

00:18:40.890 --> 00:18:42.920
the first thing came to my mind was:

00:18:42.920 --> 00:18:46.920
"If he were here,
what would your father say?"

00:18:47.630 --> 00:18:51.570
No matter how much I thought about it,
I didn't get the answer in the end.

00:18:51.570 --> 00:18:54.400
But, perhaps, I thought he would have
been bewildered and sent you off

00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:57.960
while worrying about you like I did.

00:18:58.840 --> 00:19:01.840
Tiny Sora became so big,

00:19:01.840 --> 00:19:04.940
and she found what she
wanted to do by herself.

00:19:05.380 --> 00:19:09.910
But your mother and I will
never stop worrying about you.

00:19:09.980 --> 00:19:11.470
Father...

00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:14.980
Sora, go see your mother.

00:19:16.090 --> 00:19:17.060
Yes.

00:19:26.470 --> 00:19:27.330
Sora...

00:19:28.370 --> 00:19:30.470
I scared you, didn't l?

00:19:30.470 --> 00:19:32.570
Mother, I'm sorry.

00:19:32.570 --> 00:19:35.800
Why are you apologizing?
It's not your fault.

00:19:36.080 --> 00:19:37.210
Yes it is.

00:19:37.210 --> 00:19:39.080
I said something terrible.

00:19:39.080 --> 00:19:39.880
I'm sorry.

00:19:40.410 --> 00:19:42.380
But that was not what I really think.

00:19:42.380 --> 00:19:43.180
That was...

00:19:43.320 --> 00:19:46.310
I thought I knew how anxious you were,

00:19:46.620 --> 00:19:48.490
but I said something
that drove you into a corner,

00:19:48.490 --> 00:19:51.330
and put you in a situation that you had
to say something you didn't want to.

00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:51.860
I'm sorry.

00:19:51.860 --> 00:19:52.160
Not at all.

00:19:51.860 --> 00:19:52.160
I'm sorry.

00:19:52.160 --> 00:19:52.690
Not at all.

00:19:52.690 --> 00:19:54.160
To tell you the truth,

00:19:54.160 --> 00:19:58.560
I wanted you near me
when the baby was born.

00:19:59.300 --> 00:20:02.570
After all, you are the only
big sister she has.

00:20:02.900 --> 00:20:06.670
But you said something like
"I'm not coming home" on the phone.

00:20:06.670 --> 00:20:07.910
So, I lost my composure.

00:20:07.910 --> 00:20:09.940
I told your father something selfish,

00:20:09.940 --> 00:20:13.000
saying that I'd go right over
to see you as soon as I hung up.

00:20:14.250 --> 00:20:16.220
But thanks to that, my wish came true

00:20:16.220 --> 00:20:17.550
even though it was different
from what I was expecting.

00:20:17.920 --> 00:20:19.480
Mother...

00:20:20.490 --> 00:20:23.390
Hey, come closer, Sora.

00:20:23.390 --> 00:20:24.250
Yes.

00:20:27.260 --> 00:20:29.920
Thank you for growing up a healthy girl.

00:20:31.070 --> 00:20:33.100
When we decided to adopt you,

00:20:33.100 --> 00:20:37.060
I was anxious, wondering whether
I could be your mother.

00:20:37.540 --> 00:20:40.060
I think it's the same kind of anxiety you had.

00:20:40.440 --> 00:20:43.810
When you called me "Mother"
for the first time,

00:20:43.810 --> 00:20:47.080
I was so happy and I secretly cried.

00:20:47.820 --> 00:20:52.020
Now, when you're away from me,
I worry about you.

00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:54.790
But, when I think that you're
doing fine and working hard,

00:20:54.790 --> 00:20:56.290
it makes me happy.

00:20:56.290 --> 00:20:59.730
I adore you so much, Sora.

00:20:59.730 --> 00:21:01.600
Mother...

00:21:01.600 --> 00:21:04.500
If you have any problems,
you have to tell me, at any time. Okay?

00:21:04.730 --> 00:21:05.790
Yes.

00:21:05.870 --> 00:21:07.100
Hey, Sora.

00:21:07.100 --> 00:21:08.030
What?

00:21:08.540 --> 00:21:11.030
Can you name the baby?

00:21:11.210 --> 00:21:13.170
Me? Are you sure?

00:21:13.770 --> 00:21:16.410
I always wanted you to name my baby.

00:21:16.410 --> 00:21:17.930
Okay.

00:21:18.880 --> 00:21:20.540
They said she had a healthy baby!

00:21:20.750 --> 00:21:21.280
I'm glad!

00:21:21.280 --> 00:21:22.250
Let's celebrate! Celebrate! Call everyone!

00:21:21.280 --> 00:21:22.250
I'm glad!

00:21:22.250 --> 00:21:23.850
Let's celebrate! Celebrate! Call everyone!

00:21:23.850 --> 00:21:24.720
Everyone?

00:21:24.720 --> 00:21:26.350
Who she is talking about?

00:21:26.920 --> 00:21:30.860
The Empress card also
represents childbirth.

00:21:31.130 --> 00:21:32.490
Wow... She is adorable.

00:21:32.790 --> 00:21:35.130
A little sister... Congratulations, Sora.

00:21:35.130 --> 00:21:35.960
Thank you.

00:21:35.960 --> 00:21:37.800
Thank you for everything this time.

00:21:37.800 --> 00:21:38.630
You're welcome.

00:21:38.630 --> 00:21:40.360
But we didn't do anything extraordinary.

00:21:40.800 --> 00:21:42.670
You have such a nice son.

00:21:42.840 --> 00:21:43.800
What!

00:21:43.800 --> 00:21:45.860
A nice son? Oh, well...

00:21:46.310 --> 00:21:48.870
You did a good job, little sister.

00:21:49.640 --> 00:21:50.780
I will too.

00:21:50.780 --> 00:21:53.580
I will do my best here for my dream.

00:21:54.180 --> 00:21:55.320
Oh...

00:21:55.320 --> 00:21:56.150
I decided!

00:21:56.150 --> 00:21:56.950
What?

00:21:57.020 --> 00:21:58.720
The baby's name!

00:21:58.720 --> 00:22:01.050
Yume! I want to name her Yume. "Dream."

00:22:01.520 --> 00:22:02.990
Yume...

00:22:03.220 --> 00:22:05.290
Isn't it a nice name, Father?

00:22:05.290 --> 00:22:06.960
Father?

00:22:06.960 --> 00:22:08.590
Oh... No... Well...

00:22:08.700 --> 00:22:12.190
Yume... It would be nice if she grows up fast.

00:22:20.440 --> 00:22:22.410
Next Kaleido Star

00:22:23.080 --> 00:22:25.770
I need to repay Sora's kindness a lot.

00:22:26.150 --> 00:22:29.620
And so, it's our show, a new challenge.

00:22:29.620 --> 00:22:31.720
Even though Miss Layla rejected it.

00:22:31.720 --> 00:22:33.880
To our surprise,
Rosetta came here to help us.

00:22:34.150 --> 00:22:37.420
And a mysterious shadow dashingly
appeared like the wind...

00:22:37.660 --> 00:22:40.680
Who is she really? Who? Who?

00:22:41.330 --> 00:22:43.030
Next time on Kaleido Star,
"An Amazing Change From Zero to Hero"

00:22:43.030 --> 00:22:45.430
An Amazing Change From Zero to Hero

00:22:43.030 --> 00:22:45.430
Next time on Kaleido Star,
"An Amazing Change From Zero to Hero"

00:22:45.430 --> 00:22:45.700
An Amazing Change From Zero to Hero

00:22:45.700 --> 00:22:48.290
An Amazing Change From Zero to Hero

00:22:45.700 --> 00:22:48.290
My wings are my dream
and on towards the sky...

00:22:51.470 --> 00:23:04.320
<i>Boku wa koko ni iru
sora to michi no aida de mukai kaze</i>

00:22:51.470 --> 00:23:04.320
<i>I'm here between the sky and the roads,
and facing against the wind</i>

00:23:04.320 --> 00:23:18.230
<i>Soshite mae o muiteiru,
mou nido to kanashimi ga furanai youni to</i>

00:23:04.320 --> 00:23:18.230
<i>And I'm facing forward so the sorrow
doesn't rain down ever again</i>

00:23:18.230 --> 00:23:24.170
<i>Ano kabe o koete kokomade kitanda</i>

00:23:18.230 --> 00:23:24.170
<i>I came all the way here after
I jumped over that wall</i>

00:23:24.170 --> 00:23:31.410
<i>Nigedashitaku naru koto wa nando mo aru</i>

00:23:24.170 --> 00:23:31.410
<i>There are many times
when I just want to run away</i>

00:23:31.410 --> 00:23:36.880
<i>Dakedo kokoni irunara taishite bibitte inai</i>

00:23:31.410 --> 00:23:36.880
<i>But I'm still here,
so, I'm not daunted that much</i>

00:23:36.880 --> 00:23:44.220
<i>Kakinaguri no uta "hajimekara yareba iisa"</i>

00:23:36.880 --> 00:23:44.220
<i>The poem I scribbled down, I can just
start writing over from the beginning</i>

00:23:44.220 --> 00:23:49.820
<i>Umaku kakenaku te boku wa waratte iru</i>

00:23:44.220 --> 00:23:49.820
<i>Unable to write it well, I'm laughing</i>
